+# Aegis Initial Staging Drill — Runbook (detailed)
+
+Purpose
+- Validate end-to-end orchestration in staging: control plane, safety instrumentation, evidence capture, cosign signing, Rekor registration, gRPC mTLS, energy metering, and self-healing rollback.
+
+Assumptions
+- You have a staging Kubernetes cluster named 'staging' and kubectl points to it.
+- Vault is reachable and SecretProviderClass configured to mount certs into pods.
+- Helm chart for aegis-dc has been rendered and images pushed to registry accessible by cluster.
+- COSIGN_KMS_URI and REKOR_SERVER are available to CI runner / operators.
+
+Pre-drill checks (local)
+1. Ensure helm chart values are rendered:
+   - python3 ops/helm/render_tailored_bundle.py --out /tmp/aegis_bundle --vault https://vault.staging:8200 --s3 https://minio.staging:9000 --bucket aegis-evidence-staging --rekor https://rekor.staging:3000 --dns staging.internal
+   Expected: /tmp/aegis_bundle contains rendered manifests or chart + values.generated.yaml
+
+2. Ensure SecretProviderClass is templated:
+   - sed -e "s|{{VAULT_ADDR}}|https://vault.staging:8200|" -e "s|{{VAULT_ROLE}}|aegis-grpc-server|" ops/vault/secretproviderclass-dc.yaml > /tmp/aegis_spc.yaml
+   - kubectl apply -f /tmp/aegis_spc.yaml -n aegis
+   Expected: SecretProviderClass created
+
+Deployment (staging) — apply control plane
+1. Create namespace and prerequisites:
+   - kubectl create namespace aegis || true
+   - kubectl apply -f helm/aegis-dc/templates/configmap-aegis-config.yaml -n aegis (or use rendered manifests)
+2. Deploy safety monitor and gRPC services via rendered manifests or helm:
+   - helm upgrade --install aegis-dc helm/aegis-dc -n aegis -f /tmp/aegis_bundle/values.generated.yaml
+   Expected: Deployments created; pods in Running state within 2 minutes
+3. Verify certs are mounted and services started with TLS:
+   - kubectl get pods -n aegis
+   - kubectl logs deploy/aegis-safety-monitor -n aegis
+   Expected: logs show server started; if mTLS enabled, TLS bind message present
+
+Instrumentation & injector PRs
+1. Generate injector patches and open PRs (dry-run first):
+   - python3 ops/autonomy/run_injector_and_generate_diffs.py --paths services controllers --out /tmp/patches
+   Expected: patches in /tmp/patches/*.patch
+2. Apply injector patches in draft PRs (operator-run):
+   - DO_OPEN_PR=true python3 ops/autonomy/apply_injector_and_create_prs.py --paths services controllers --branch-prefix inject/safety
+   Expected: Draft PRs opened for reviewers
+
+Functional test: canary promotion & evidence capture
+1. Trigger a canary promotion (simulate):
+   - kubectl exec -n aegis deploy/safety-monitor -- python3 -c "from ops.autonomy.safety_monitor import check_and_allow, record_manifest; print(check_and_allow('canary_promote', {'who':'drill'})); print(record_manifest('drill_canary','{}'))"
+   Expected: check_and_allow returns True (if OPA allows), record_manifest returns manifest path or queued path
+2. Validate evidence queue and uploader:
+   - kubectl exec -n aegis deploy/safety-monitor -- ls -la /tmp/evidence_pending || true
+   - kubectl exec -n aegis deploy/safety-monitor -- python3 ops/evidence/uploader.py || true
+   Expected: Manifest uploaded to S3 and Rekor (or queued on failure)
+3. Check Rekor registration:
+   - rekor-cli search --artifact <manifest-path> --server https://rekor.staging:3000
+   Expected: Rekor entry found (or pending if Rekor temporarily unavailable)
+
+DP / MPC gating test
+1. Attempt to enable MPC without audit:
+   - kubectl exec -n aegis deploy/safety-monitor -- python3 -c "from ops.autonomy.safety_monitor import check_and_allow; print(check_and_allow('enable_mpc', {}))"
+   Expected: returns False and a manifest recorded indicating block
+2. Update config/audit_status.yaml to approve MPC (only after crypto audit) and verify check_and_allow allows enable_mpc
+
+Chaos & liveness test
+1. Run chaos harness in staging:
+   - python3 ops/chaos/chaos_harness.py
+   Expected: chaos report at /tmp/chaos_report.json showing rollback and evidence manifests
+2. Aggregate multiple runs:
+   - python3 ops/chaos/continuous_chaos_runner.py
+   Expected: /tmp/chaos_runs/aggregate.json with run count and reports
+
+Energy & carbon test
+1. Run a short training job via wrapper:
+   - ./ops/carbon/job_wrapper.sh "sleep 10" 1 carbon
+   Expected: job_energy manifest in /tmp and Prometheus textfile updated
+2. Verify Prometheus exporter:
+   - kubectl exec -n aegis deploy/prometheus -- python3 ops/monitoring/carbon_prometheus_exporter.py
+   Expected: aegis_total_co2_kg, aegis_total_energy_kwh files written to textfile collector dir
+
+Recovery & incident simulation
+1. Simulate evidence pipeline outage:
+   - stop rekor or block network to evidence S3 then run a canary promotion
+   Expected: manifest placed in /tmp/evidence_pending
+2. Run recovery helper:
+   - python3 ops/verify/incident_recovery_helper.py
+   Expected: attempts to re-sign and upload, writes /tmp/evidence_recovery.log
+
+Post-drill verification
+1. Ensure evidence_coverage == 100% displayed in Level-4 verification report
+   - python3 ops/verify/level4_verification.sh --evidence-bucket <bucket>
+2. Collect and produce auditor bundle:
+   - python3 ops/autonomy/generate_auditor_zip.py --out /tmp/aegis_audit_bundle.tar.gz
+   Expected: tar.gz with artifacts, cosign signed (if COSIGN_KMS_URI present)
+
+Rollback & cleanup
+1. If everything passes, keep deployed components for further staging tests or tear down:
+   - helm uninstall aegis-dc -n aegis
+   - kubectl delete namespace aegis
+
+Contacts & escalation
+- Platform owner: platform@your-org
+- Security on-call: security@your-org
+- Compliance: compliance@your-org
